# report/figures — the one log-log figure of the study

This directory is figtab-repo's package in the work assignment
(`assignment.json` in world/story-repo): exactly one figure,
`mae_loglog.png`, the log-log plot of the error with the fit that the
research objective requires for `report/report.md`.

## The claim the figure supports

The mean absolute error (MAE) of the Monte Carlo pi estimate falls with
the sample count N like N^b, and the fitted exponent b is consistent with
the -1/2 expected for Monte Carlo methods.

## What is drawn

- Points: MAE = mean of |pi_hat - pi| over the 200 independent runs at each
  required N (10^3 .. 10^7), with +/-1 SE error bars from the table's
  `se_mean_absolute_error` column.
- Solid line: the OLS fit of ln(MAE) vs ln(N) taken from experiment-repo's
  committed `analysis/fit.json` (never recomputed here); the slope b is in
  the legend, and the line is cross-checked against the committed
  `fit_mae` column before rendering.
- Dashed line: the asymptotic (large-N) theoretical expectation,
  `normal_approximation_mae` = sqrt(2(4-pi)) * N^(-1/2), drawn from the
  CSV column (an analytic prediction, not fitted; the normal approximation
  of the exact binomial MAE, which is the `exact_binomial_mae` column and
  the table's "analytic expectation").
- Annotation box: b, the headline 95% interval (residual OLS Student-t,
  df=3, the settled primary), the dependence-aware check (paired bootstrap
  over runs, shown side by side), whether -1/2 lies inside, and the method
  facts (200 runs per N, seeds `default_rng(2026 + run_index)`).

## Inputs (all numbers come from these, nothing is recomputed)

From experiment-repo at a recorded commit:

- `analysis/mae_table.csv` — columns N, mean_absolute_error,
  se_mean_absolute_error, normal_approximation_mae, exact_binomial_mae,
  fit_mae (aliases are matched case-insensitively; see the key lists at
  the top of `plot_mae_loglog.py`).
- `analysis/fit.json` — the OLS slope and intercept, and the two 95%
  intervals under the settled priority: `headline_interval` (residual OLS
  Student-t) and `paired_bootstrap` (dependence-aware check); legacy key
  names (primary_interval / ols_t_sensitivity) still map onto these roles.

If a key name is not recognized the script warns on stderr and lists what
it found; extend the aliases in one place rather than editing data.

## Rendering

    python3 plot_mae_loglog.py --inputs <experiment-repo checkout> \
        [--outdir <this directory>]

This writes `mae_loglog.png` plus two files beside it:

- `caption.md` — an embeddable figure caption with the actual numbers,
  for paper-repo to use in `report/report.md`.
- `provenance.json` — the input repo, commit, paths and SHA256 of each
  input file, the values used, the environment versions and the command.

Pipeline self-test (synthetic data, stamped SELF-TEST, never for
delivery):

    python3 plot_mae_loglog.py --selftest /tmp/selftest.png

The rendering is inspected programmatically with `check_render.py` in this
repository's root (log-log axes, the five points' values checked exactly
against the CSV, error bars, line slopes against fit.json and the theory
column, legend, annotation content and placement, no overlaps, PNG size
and ink coverage, provenance commit/SHA256). This session's model cannot
view images, so artist- and pixel-level inspection is the recorded method.

